⭐ Final Recommended Solution

For LeetCode 641, use the Circular Array + front + rear + size approach.

The key formulas to memorize:

Move Front Forward
front = (front + 1) % capacity;
Move Front Backward
front = (front - 1 + capacity) % capacity;
Move Rear Forward
rear = (rear + 1) % capacity;
Move Rear Backward
rear = (rear - 1 + capacity) % capacity;

And remember this implementation's convention:

front → first element
rear  → position after last element

Therefore:

getFront() = dequeue[front]

while:

getRear() = dequeue[(rear - 1 + capacity) % capacity]
